%T A401356 4832129,4832129,4832129,4832129,4832129,12308321,75720089,75720089,
%U A401356 826931681,826931681,826931681,5478296321,9701757521,9701757521,9701757521,9701757521,9701757521,9701757521
%N A401356 Least number congruent to 17 modulo 24 that is a quadratic residue modulo the first n-1 primes greater than 3.
%C A401356 Let N = A102476(n+2) be the least modulus with 2^(n+2) square roots of 1. a(n) is the minimal element of the coset of (Z/NZ)*^2 in (Z/NZ)* containing A402500(n+1) = N/3 + 1 or 2*N/3 + 1, or the least m coprime to N such that A402500(n+1)/m is a square modulo N. Here (Z/NZ)* is the multiplicative group of integers modulo N and (Z/NZ)*^2 is the subgroup of squares.
%C A401356 For each n, while a(n) is a square in R, Q_2 and in Q_p for 5 <= p <= prime(n+1), Q_3 is a witness of a(n) being a nonsquare (i.e., a(n) is not a (local) square in Q_3). Sequences -A045535, A401305, A402507, and A402547 are similar constructions (see A401305).
%C A401356 For any fundamental discriminant D of a quadratic field dividing N, kronecker(D,a(n)) = -1 if and only if 3 divides D.
%e A401356 The cosets of (Z/NZ)*^2 in (Z/NZ)* containing A402500(n+1) = N/2 + 1, with N = A102476(n+2) for n=1..4:
%e A401356   {17}
%e A401356   {41, 89}
%e A401356   {281, 401, 449, 569, 641, 809}
%e A401356   {401, 449, 641, 1241, 1409, 1961, 2249, 2489, 3089, 3161, 3809, 4481, 4601, 4841, 5009, 5681, 6161, 6329, 6449, 6521, 6689, 7001, 7121, 7529, 7841, 8009, 8369, 8801, 8849, 8969}
%o A401356 (PARI) a(n, st=17) = my(P = prime(n+1)); forstep(k=st, oo, 24, forprime(p=5, P, if(kronecker(k, p)<1, next(2))); return(k)) \\ st == 17 (mod 24) allows to calculate a(n) if a(n-1) is known
%Y A401356 Cf. A102476, A402500.
%Y A401356 See A402499 for a list of related sequences.
%K A401356 nonn,new
%O A401356 1,1
%A A401356 _Jianing Song_, Nov 20 2026
